{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments","id":1146419,"title":"Alternate Arcana Attainments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-03T13:08:21-07:00","id":1146419,"title":"Alternate Arcana Attainments","content":"I'm pretty dissatisfied with the Forces arcana attainments, so I think a do over is in order.<br /> <br /> The changes I'm making:<br /> <br /> Forces 2: Spend a mana to gain Sensory Range on Forces spells. You can thank the smug sidebar that mentions how dangerous working with Forces can be for this change.<br /> <br /> Forces 4: There's no reason at all that you shouldn't be able to enter a CoW if someone casts a direct Forces spell at you at this level. So I'm adding that to the original attainment. <br /> <br /> While I'm at it:<br /> <br /> Matter 4: Changing the Durability of an object is really lackluster, especially since the change only lasts a Scene. To be fair to whoever made this attainment, we didn't have Perfected Materials yet. Instead, a Mage with Matter 4 can Perfect a material without the use of Twilight or a spell. Right now I'm toying with the idea that it modifies Mage Sight when using Scrutiny on an object. Treat the Size, Durability, or Structure (Whichever is greater) as the Opacity of the Mystery (Material to be Perfected). This must be performed in a Demesne, Verge, or other appropriately resonant location for the task of Perfecting. Times between Scrutiny rolls are an hour as you're not just studying the material, but slowly teasing the imperfections of its existence out of it. Mana can be spent as usual to accrue more successes. Once the Opacity is reduced to 0, roll a Revelation to &quot;cap&quot; the process. The transformation is permanent. This method of Perfecting cannot be used on energies such as Fire, or on living materials such as blood or flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T15:49:54-07:00","id":1146465,"title":"","content":"Yeah the Forces attainments are definitly... lackluster to say the least. I agree with your assessment of Forces 4, it should entitle you to a CoW and your thoughts on Matter 4 are also interesting. I'm not sure about Forces 2 though....<br /> <br /> Forces 2: What is the metaphysical reasoning here though? Time and Space do it because they help with reaches that literally touch upon their purviews. Matter can do it for Matter because to be enduring is distinctly a property of matter, even when Matter changes in the end there will allways be matter left over. How does Forces relate to sensory range? Is it because all of our senses are related to forces? Makes sense from an anthropological viewpoint but in mage the truth is not necessarily constrained by a human perspective. For now it seems to me that range is mostly a seperation of space, not purview of Forces. On the other hand Forces may be king when it comes to spells that enhance the range of your senses (see &quot;Zoom In&quot;). I like the idea, I'm just not fully convinced of the metaphysics yet.<br /> <br /> Here's an alternative that came to mind: Forces releases alot of Force but doesn't last long. By spending a point of mana the mage can add 2 to the potency of a Forces spell, however the spell cannot reach for advanced duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 10-03-2017, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T16:03:37-07:00","id":1146471,"title":"","content":"The reason for Sensory Range is as I said because of the sidebar on pg. 141:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Many Forces effects are just as harmful to the<br /> mage herself as they are to any potential victims.<br /> If the mage does not Reach to cast them at sensory<br /> range, she could just as easily electrocute or<br /> incinerate herself in the process. Some effects are<br /> beneficial enough that the mage need not worry<br /> about harming herself, such as warming a cold<br /> area or lighting a dark room, but proper caution<br /> is advised when conjuring fire, explosions, electricity,<br /> and other such destructive forces. </div> </div> </div>This sidebar is basically saying that Sensory Range is required to use Forces safely, if it's going to be required then it makes sense that Forces Mages would develop such a propensity for using Forces at Sensory Range that they learn to spend just a mana to make it happen instead of a Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T16:33:51-07:00","id":1146480,"title":"","content":"Attainments aren't about what would be useful for that particular arcarnum, they're effects that logically stem from a deep understanding of it. Nothing in forces logically lends itself to being able to cast at greater range. If anything that is an alternate form a space attainment could take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T16:41:10-07:00","id":1146483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1146480#post1146480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attainments aren't about what would be useful for that particular arcarnum, they're effects that logically stem from a deep understanding of it. Nothing in forces logically lends itself to being able to cast at greater range. If anything that is an alternate form a space attainment could take.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Attainments are magical effects, similar to spells but not subject</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">to the same rules. They allow a mage to employ meta-magical</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">effects in order to improve the efficacy of her Arcana and change</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">the world around her in lasting ways.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bYeah, I think the text disagrees with you. It doesn't say anything about it needing to be thematically appropriate to the arcana, and to my mind, easing the use of Forces at Sensory Range certainly would be thematically appropriate to boot.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T16:50:12-07:00","id":1146485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1146483#post1146483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bYeah, I think the text disagrees with you. It doesn't say anything about it needing to be thematically appropriate to the arcana</div> </div> </div> </div>That passage is not the reason I believe that attainments need to be thematically appropriate to the arcarna. I think that because <i>every single fucking attainment in the fucking book is thematically appropriate to it's arcarnum.</i> It's called pattern recognition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T16:58:50-07:00","id":1146489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1146485#post1146485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That passage is not the reason I believe that attainments need to be thematically appropriate to the arcarna. I think that because <i>every single fucking attainment in the fucking book is thematically appropriate to it's arcarnum.</i> It's called pattern recognition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you understood why I used the quote. I was backing up my claim via the text, which is to say that this explicit piece of text is a superior piece of evidence to your implied evidence. Oh, and I think that a Sensory Range attainment is thematically appropriate to Forces too, and fits your &quot;pattern recognition&quot; requirement. So I don't know what you're getting so bilious for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T17:15:37-07:00","id":1146491,"title":"","content":"By the same logic, though, it would also make sense for Mages with an understanding in Forces to develop ways to handle spells. I feel like throwing a lightning javelin or tossing a fireball is thematically appropriate too, which would require use of being able to hold that energy without hurting oneself. Hmmm....<br /> <br /> So, what about this:<br /> <br /> A Forces apprentice has learned how to shield himself from the naturally harmful energies that he has been working with. A Forces apprentice can spend a dram of mana as he is casting to protect himself from the energies his spell. This protection lasts until the spell dissipates or until the end of the scene, whichever comes first.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T17:29:13-07:00","id":1146495,"title":"","content":"That's not a bad alternative. I like doing Sensory Range because it's only a slight variation on existing rules for attainments. Doing something like that would allow you to reach into a fire and grab a handful of the stuff to hurl at a foe or direct where you will though. I like it, except it feels a bit like a cheat, like if you got Alchemist's Touch as an attainment at Matter 2 and better damage reduction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T18:05:00-07:00","id":1146508,"title":"","content":"Well, it only works for your own spells, and you have to spend a mana per spell to shield yourself, so it's not quite as useful as a shielding spell. That being said it can save you a spell slot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T18:13:39-07:00","id":1146509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1146489#post1146489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I don't know what you're getting so bilious for.</div> </div> </div> </div>You opened this thread by calling the sidebar in question &quot;smug.&quot; Let's not pretend to impartial presentation here.<br /> <br /> The trouble with Sensory Range is that it removes one of the other big dangers of using Forces right out the gate, i.e. using a spell at range without Reaching for it means you have to use Area Scale and risk the effects of an already volatile Arcanum propagating through the usual caveat about what things are Lasting. &quot;Spend a Mana instead of a Reach&quot; translates to, among other things, &quot;Spend a Mana instead of [Paradox dice] Mana&quot; for effects that push your limits.<br /> <br /> The Lesser Utility Attainment for Life enhances Pattern Restoration; suppose Forces enhanced the effects of flaring your Nimbus?<br /> <br /> For that matter, the Lesser Utility Attainment for Matter makes Advanced Duration easier; suppose Forces had greater access to Advanced Potency?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T19:27:42-07:00","id":1146526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1146509#post1146509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You opened this thread by calling the sidebar in question &amp;quot;smug.&amp;quot; Let's not pretend to impartial presentation here.<br /> <br /> The trouble with Sensory Range is that it removes one of the other big dangers of using Forces right out the gate, i.e. using a spell at range without Reaching for it means you have to use Area Scale and risk the effects of an already volatile Arcanum propagating through the usual caveat about what things are Lasting. &amp;quot;Spend a Mana instead of a Reach&amp;quot; translates to, among other things, &amp;quot;Spend a Mana instead of [Paradox dice] Mana&amp;quot; for effects that push your limits.<br /> <br /> The Lesser Utility Attainment for Life enhances Pattern Restoration; suppose Forces enhanced the effects of flaring your Nimbus?<br /> <br /> For that matter, the Lesser Utility Attainment for Matter makes Advanced Duration easier; suppose Forces had greater access to Advanced Potency?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t recall saying that I was making an impartial presentation. That said, I\u2019m not using caustic language (Maybe slightly abrasive) against those whom I might disagree with. Basically, feel free to disagree, but keep it civil, and definitely, don\u2019t presume I haven\u2019t read and familiarized myself with these rules and their patterns, etc. and then take a condescending tone. <br /> <br /> Now, on to the rest: I\u2019m aware that allowing Sensory Range for a mana removes most of the danger of the use of Forces. That\u2019s rather why I think that Mages over the untold ages they\u2019ve had access to Forces would have developed a safer alternative. It also doesn\u2019t lessen the inherent Hubris in the use of Forces for any number of things except in that it\u2019s no longer necessary to pay the Reach tax of casting at Sensory to keep from being burned. If anything, it encourages you to control the fire to burn the bad guy because it\u2019s a \u201csafer\u201d and easier route.<br /> <br /> Your two examples of increased effect to Nimbus or Potency are well taken, but again I wanted to deviate from existing rules as little as possible. That makes your advancement of Potency the more compelling case, but it suffers from being very niche. The only instance in which it might matter is if someone entered a Forces CoW, or attempts to Dispel it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T20:30:38-07:00","id":1146548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1146526#post1146526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your two examples of increased effect to Nimbus or Potency are well taken, but again I wanted to deviate from existing rules as little as possible. That makes your advancement of Potency the more compelling case, but it suffers from being very niche. The only instance in which it might matter is if someone entered a Forces CoW, or attempts to Dispel it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, this <i>would</i> be coming at the same level of Forces as Control Weather and Environmental Shield open up, and Forces is pretty well-stocked with effects that are likely to contend with Counterspelling compared to less energetic Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T02:00:29-07:00","id":1146590,"title":"","content":"The passage describing the attainments not mentioning that they have to be thematically appropriate<i> isn't </i>evidence against the notion that they should be <i>at all</i>, because <i>why the hell would it</i>? It's just an intro telling you what they do, not guidelines for making your own. They're all pre-made. We're not supposed to make our own, and so specifying the design parameters would just be a waste of wordcount.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-04-2017, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T03:12:32-07:00","id":1146595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1146590#post1146590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The passage describing the attainments not mentioning that they have to be thematically appropriate<i> isn't </i>evidence against the notion that they should be <i>at all</i>, because <i>why the hell would it</i>? It's just an intro telling you what they do, not guidelines for making your own. They're all pre-made. We're not supposed to make our own, and so specifying the design parameters would just be a waste of wordcount.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know if you\u2019ve noticed, but sprinkled here and there throughout all of the CoD game line are words like, \u201cYou can use this as is or change it.\u201d<br /> <br /> In fact under the 2-dot Arcana Attainment header is the sentence, \u201cBelow are some of the most common Lesser Utilities, though the players and the Storytellers may devise others.\u201d<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t know what you\u2019re talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T03:33:27-07:00","id":1146598,"title":"","content":"Ok, I admittedly missed that. But <i>you </i>seem to have missed the sentence <i>\u200bdirectly preceding it:<br /> <br /> </i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lesser Utilities are Attainments that <b>fit into the purview of the Arcana</b>, but don\u2019t map to the Practices and rely more on a general understanding of the Arcanum in question than of specific spells. </div> </div> </div>And I'm sorry, but mucking about with range is <i>definitely </i>a Space thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T03:47:05-07:00","id":1146601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1146598#post1146598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I admittedly missed that. But <i>you </i>seem to have missed the sentence [I]\u200bdirectly preceding it:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And I'm sorry, but mucking about with range is <i>definitely </i>a Space thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I already said, I believe it does fit. Forces has plenty of range expanding tricks already like Zoom In.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T03:49:00-07:00","id":1146602,"title":"","content":"Zoom In is a light bending trick. That's totally in Forces wheelhouse. What aspect of Forces inherently lends itself to &quot;far away from me&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T03:54:52-07:00","id":1146606,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure you\u2019re looking at this the right way, it\u2019s not about \u201cfar away from me\u201d, it\u2019s about not touching the dangerous energies they control. The sidebar is the text going out of its way to point out that Sensory Range is basically a requirement for using Forces which puts Sensory Range inside Forces wheelhouse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T03:59:29-07:00","id":1146607,"title":"","content":"Range complements Forces nicely, but that doesn't mean range is part of Forces' purview. Just because Sensory Range is particularly useful for Forces (or even a requirement for some Forces spells) doesn't mean increased range is an inherent part of the Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T04:03:13-07:00","id":1146608,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I really don't think that's how it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T04:14:32-07:00","id":1146611,"title":"","content":"If you need a battery to make a thing work, almost all of the time the battery will be considered part of the thing its powering. The battery in this case is Sensory Range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T04:33:50-07:00","id":1146613,"title":"","content":"It's not about being part of it, it's about being able to create the battery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T04:34:59-07:00","id":1146614,"title":"","content":"That's not how Arcana work, though. I repeat, just because something is useful for one Arcanum doesn't mean it's part of that Arcanum.<br /> Now, if you want to base Arcana Attainments on utility rather than purviews, be my guest. In that case I'd support your suggestion since it does make sense that mages that deal with Forces do want an easier time using Sensory Range. But nothing in electricity, gravity, radiation, sound, light, heat, fire, weather, or movement implies that extended range is a direct part of Forces.<br /> <br /> Besides, if I want to buy batteries I don't go to a camera store just because cameras are useless without them. I either go to a general store (i.e. use a Reach) or to an electronics store where batteries are a natural part of their range of products (i.e. put the sensory range Attainment where it actually makes sense: Space).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-04-2017, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T05:10:10-07:00","id":1146625,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> It is called a Lesser Utility after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T05:14:40-07:00","id":1146627,"title":"","content":"If that's what you want. But you did argue that your suggestion fit this piece of text: &quot;Lesser Utilities are Attainments that fit into the purview of the Arcana&quot;. That's what I was opposing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-04-2017, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T07:42:34-07:00","id":1146656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1146607#post1146607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Range complements Forces nicely, but that doesn't mean range is part of Forces' purview. Just because Sensory Range is particularly useful for Forces (or even a requirement for some Forces spells) doesn't mean increased range is an inherent part of the Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. So much this. A good example of how a Forces based attainment could compliment the senses: Spend one mana, multiply the sensititvity (&quot;range&quot;) of your sight and hearing by your Forces rating for the rest of the scene. (or perhaps rather a flat amount as utility attainments usually don't work off of the Arcanum rating.) That makes thematically sense as it interacts with Forces. Also Satchels suggestion of spending Mana instead of a reach for advanced potency makes sense (I do admit that with advanced potency being less generally useful than many other reaches it's less attractive) or my own where you get + potency on spells without long duration. Those make sense thematically, as it increases the &quot;Force&quot;/power of your spell. Sure the mystic potency is more a purview of Prime than Forces, but the Forces arcanum itself resonates with power, so it makes sense thematically in the end.<br /> <br /> And yes it is never outright stated that an attainment needs to be thematically connected to the Arcanum in question. But it makes sense. Every other attainment published is. In fact the whole magic system is working within thematic logic. In fact magic in MtAw is entirely reliant on symbolism. The supernal realms themselves literally are a collection of symbols and thus all power derived from them works through symbolism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure you\u2019re looking at this the right way, it\u2019s not about \u201cfar away from me\u201d, it\u2019s about not touching the dangerous energies they control. The sidebar is the text going out of its way to point out that Sensory Range is basically a requirement for using Forces which puts Sensory Range inside Forces wheelhouse. </div> </div> </div>No. The sidebar points out a problem you can encounter when relying on using the Forces Arcanum. It's a difficulty and they probably would not point it out if it was supposed to be easily circumvented with a lesser utility attainment. And the logic in that quote is very much off, if it's a requirement for using Forces it's not part of its purview, it's a requirement. Again <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> put it well, a battery isn't under the purview of cameras just because cameras need them to function.<br /> <br /> That said it's a rather interesting topic in general and some of the attainments have irked me in the past, so maybe I should write some homebrew for this myself next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T07:58:41-07:00","id":1146662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1146606#post1146606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure you\u2019re looking at this the right way, it\u2019s not about \u201cfar away from me\u201d, it\u2019s about not touching the dangerous energies they control. The sidebar is the text going out of its way to point out that Sensory Range is basically a requirement for using Forces which puts Sensory Range inside Forces wheelhouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sidebar is the text going out of its way to point out that Forces pose a dramatically more immediate danger to the mage commanding them.<br /> <br /> Aimed Spells don't pop their effects before they hit their targets, but Forces spells have a higher likelihood of being effecting in ways that don't require direct &quot;core&quot; contact with something to deal collateral damage. It's not &quot;throwing a fireball will inevitably burn you,&quot; it's &quot;throwing a fireball may set things on fire other than what you intended.&quot;<br /> <br /> Further, Sensory Range isn't just &quot;the effect doesn't touch you,&quot; it's &quot;the effect manifests on top of the target and stays with it even if it moves&quot; and &quot;with an additional Reach, you can target something you're viewing remotely.&quot; That's <i>maybe</i> useful to the Arcanum dealing with effects that tend to propagate, but it's not especially fitting as the more-accessible unique benefit of that Arcanum any more than Time In A Bottle would be suitable as a Lesser Utility Attainment.<br /> <br /> Permanency makes sense as a Matter Attainment because its effect is just &quot;changes you make with Matter last longer with less effort.&quot; Cutting out half the cost of remote casting because you think the dangers of magical arson stem from something besides being on the same block as your spell doesn't track similarly; Forces is a Reach-intensive Arcanum to use directly and in-person with or without a Range modifier, because it's thematically one of the loudest of the Gross Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T16:42:01-07:00","id":1146845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1146662#post1146662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sidebar is the text going out of its way to point out that Forces pose a dramatically more immediate danger to the mage commanding them.<br /> <br /> Aimed Spells don't pop their effects before they hit their targets, but Forces spells have a higher likelihood of being effecting in ways that don't require direct &quot;core&quot; contact with something to deal collateral damage. It's not &quot;throwing a fireball will inevitably burn you,&quot; it's &quot;throwing a fireball may set things on fire other than what you intended.&quot;<br /> <br /> Further, Sensory Range isn't just &quot;the effect doesn't touch you,&quot; it's &quot;the effect manifests on top of the target and stays with it even if it moves&quot; and &quot;with an additional Reach, you can target something you're viewing remotely.&quot; That's <i>maybe</i> useful to the Arcanum dealing with effects that tend to propagate, but it's not especially fitting as the more-accessible unique benefit of that Arcanum any more than Time In A Bottle would be suitable as a Lesser Utility Attainment.<br /> <br /> Permanency makes sense as a Matter Attainment because its effect is just &quot;changes you make with Matter last longer with less effort.&quot; Cutting out half the cost of remote casting because you think the dangers of magical arson stem from something besides being on the same block as your spell doesn't track similarly; Forces is a Reach-intensive Arcanum to use directly and in-person with or without a Range modifier, because it's thematically one of the loudest of the Gross Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence my idea of an attainment that allows you to protect yourself from the effects of your spells.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T16:58:42-07:00","id":1146852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1146845#post1146845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hence my idea of an attainment that allows you to protect yourself from the effects of your spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only problem with this is that you don\u2019t need protection from your spells as much as you need protection from the subjects of your spells.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> when Permanence was revealed people flipped their shit and declared it OP. If you\u2019re going to use that as an example of something that \u201cmakes sense\u201d then for my house rule I\u2019m just going to say wait. Sensory Range could be described as emanations of will exerted on the subject in mimicry of the influence of sunlight or gravity from the moon on Earth. The BS thematic explanation is available with a little creativity. Mechanically, I think it\u2019s an asshole move to have one arcana that has what basically amounts to a Reach tax applied to it just because it\u2019s \u201cvolatile.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T18:15:42-07:00","id":1146872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1146852#post1146852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when Permanence was revealed people flipped their shit and declared it OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>When Permanence was revealed we didn't have the entire core system available to us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sensory Range could be described as emanations of will exerted on the subject in mimicry of the influence of sunlight or gravity from the moon on Earth. The BS thematic explanation is available with a little creativity. </div> </div> </div>The BS thematic explanation you're using does not correspond to Sensory Range. The BS thematic explanation you're using corresponds to Aimed Spells being projectiles and emanations. You could certainly do something with boosting your range with Aimed Forces Spells, but no amount of comparison to vector-based phenomena is going to translate to &quot;the spell skips the intervening distance altogether.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mechanically, I think it\u2019s an asshole move to have one arcana that has what basically amounts to a Reach tax applied to it just because it\u2019s \u201cvolatile.\u201d </div> </div> </div>Mechanically, few other Arcana have the advantage of being <i>omnipresent and versatile</i>. Circumstances in which you have no Forces to work with all but require extremely weird outliers like the periphery of a Scar leading to a Lower Depth.<br /> <br /> Forces needs a lot of care to use safely and subtly and getting the ability to brush off that risk as soon as you become an Apprentice takes away from the ramifications of going loud with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 10-04-2017, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T10:10:28-07:00","id":1147090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1146852#post1146852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sensory Range could be described as emanations of will exerted on the subject in mimicry of the influence of sunlight or gravity from the moon on Earth.<br /> The BS thematic explanation is available with a little creativity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just sounds like you're trying to force your ideas to fit within a theme rather than actually going with the theme. It's also not very cleanly argued, as Satchel allready pointed out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mechanically, I think it\u2019s an asshole move to have one arcana that has what basically amounts to a Reach tax applied to it just because it\u2019s \u201cvolatile.\u201d </div> </div> </div>Um no. Forces doesn't have a reach tax. You want to use Forces without sensory range? Go ahead. You want to control fire? Well you can cast that at touch range if you cast a fire shielding spell beforehand. That's unfair? Tell it to the Moros handling Chlorine gas over there, he cast Alchemists Touch beforehand and you don't hear him bitch about it. You can easily touch all kinds of nonvolatile Forces, like Gravity, Light etc. The problem is that you often want to affect stuff &quot;over there&quot;. Well that's a problem all the Arcana suffer from. Attainments offer awesome abilities, but they do so within a theme and sensory range is not part of Forces theme. It being useful towards using Forces doesn't make it part of its theme. The Forces 2 attainment is very lackluster as it is, but a replacement should make sense within the setting and shouldn't just be what seems to be most useful. Attainments are not about usefulness, they are about intrinsic extensions of the Arcanums theme.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T00:13:58-07:00","id":1207565,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Yeeeah, I also disagree with your argument of Sensory Range being in the purview of Forces. It's more of a Space thing. That being said, I've come up with a similar Forces Attainment:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#bf9000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\">[Lesser Attainment] Forces: Focused Blast</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Fire and lightning is just as dangerous for the mage wielding them as it is for their enemies, so it pays for the Apprentice of Forces to fire their spells at a safe distance. With practice in Forces, the mage can fire such spells more easily.</span></span> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>System:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Whenever the mage casts an Aimed spell with Forces as its highest Arcanum, they add their Forces dots to the aiming roll.</span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sensory Range doesn't make sense, but focusing the accuracy of an Aimed Forces spell certainly does. Sure, it's not Sensory Range, but it doesn't cost any Mana either.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T01:47:48-07:00","id":1207583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1207565#post1207565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Yeeeah, I also disagree with your argument of Sensory Range being in the purview of Forces. It's more of a Space thing. That being said, I've come up with a similar Forces Attainment:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#bf9000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\">[Lesser Attainment] Forces: Focused Blast</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Fire and lightning is just as dangerous for the mage wielding them as it is for their enemies, so it pays for the Apprentice of Forces to fire their spells at a safe distance. With practice in Forces, the mage can fire such spells more easily.</span></span> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>System:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Whenever the mage casts an Aimed spell with Forces as its highest Arcanum, they add their Forces dots to the aiming roll.</span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sensory Range doesn't make sense, but focusing the accuracy of an Aimed Forces spell certainly does. Sure, it's not Sensory Range, but it doesn't cost any Mana either.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>I came up with the same idea. Improving aim and altering the course of your &quot;spell-projectile&quot; in flight seems well in the purview of forces. I would let it cost Mana though and add flat 3 dice to the pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T02:33:45-07:00","id":1207590,"title":"","content":"I wonder, how about a Forces Utility Attainment that specifically treats only stuff under Forces\u2019 purview as being at touch range for purposes of spellcasting, instead of outright giving sensory range? Probably Forces 4, since it sounds like an advanced application of telekinetic stuff, which are at Forces 3 to 4.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The logic being that, Forces being an inherently emanating phenomena, the mage\u2019s own will and aptitude serves as its medium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T03:01:45-07:00","id":1207597,"title":"","content":"I, on the other hand, agree that Sensory range seems in theme with Forces for an Attainment. It is <i>Sensory</i> Range, and senses rely upon forces for operation. You are more binding the effect to the forces you are using for perception than employing a distance negating hack. (Another justification is that you are projecting the effect with more &quot;force&quot;, enabling it to reach farther)<br /> <br /> The argument that exploiting the mechanisms by with senses are used is &quot;unthematic&quot; with Mage's use of Symbolism runs into its other theme of Understanding How Things <i>Really</i> Work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T07:58:03-07:00","id":1207660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1207597#post1207597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, on the other hand, agree that Sensory range seems in theme with Forces for an Attainment. It is <i>Sensory</i> Range, and senses rely upon forces for operation. You are more binding the effect to the forces you are using for perception than employing a distance negating hack. (Another justification is that you are projecting the effect with more &quot;force&quot;, enabling it to reach farther)<br /> <br /> The argument that exploiting the mechanisms by with senses are used is &quot;unthematic&quot; with Mage's use of Symbolism runs into its other theme of Understanding How Things <i>Really</i> Work.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that vein, all the Gross Arcana could be used to access sensory range. ... Which, now that I think about it, isn\u2019t necessarily a bad thing. <br /> <br /> However, sensory range as a spell factor, not in its literal meaning of the physical distance up to your sensory organs can pick up sensory input or vice-versa, remains a Space thing due to granting spells a \u201choming\u201d ability, and being a stepping stone to remote viewing and Sympathetic Range/ Temporal Sympathy. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, I have an idea for a Forces Attainment allowing you to use energy emanated from your body or an object in your person as an extension for touch range for purposes of Forces spells. Singing a flame into dancing, using a laser pointer to heat up and spontaneously combust someone from afar, silencing an area where the light of the torch you carry shines on, that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T08:40:40-07:00","id":1207663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1207660#post1207660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In that vein, all the Gross Arcana could be used to access sensory range. ... Which, now that I think about it, isn\u2019t necessarily a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much, I'd think. Time and Life are harder to work &quot;through&quot;. Matter is fair, and Space, we are already comparing this to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1207660#post1207660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, sensory range as a spell factor, not in its literal meaning of the physical distance up to your sensory organs can pick up sensory input or vice-versa, remains a Space thing due to granting spells a \u201choming\u201d ability, and being a stepping stone to remote viewing and Sympathetic Range/ Temporal Sympathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm seeing more as &quot;sending the spell via light/soundwaves&quot;. If someone hides behind a paper curtain, that would block sensory perception, and thus this Attainment (from my perspective). Space, on the other hand, doesn't care what is between caster and target, because it outright ignores the distance. That is the distinction I'm focusing on for the above logic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1207660#post1207660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, I have an idea for a Forces Attainment allowing you to use energy emanated from your body or an object in your person as an extension for touch range for purposes of Forces spells. Singing a flame into dancing, using a laser pointer to heat up and spontaneously combust someone from afar, silencing an area where the light of the torch you carry shines on, that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems more like an Imbued Item. Idea is conveying &quot;touch&quot; via an energy medium, right? &quot;Spooky action at a distance&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T14:32:44-07:00","id":1207757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1207663#post1207663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not so much, I'd think. Time and Life are harder to work &amp;quot;through&amp;quot;. Matter is fair, and Space, we are already comparing this to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm seeing more as &amp;quot;sending the spell via light/soundwaves&amp;quot;. If someone hides behind a paper curtain, that would block sensory perception, and thus this Attainment (from my perspective). Space, on the other hand, doesn't care what is between caster and target, because it outright ignores the distance. That is the distinction I'm focusing on for the above logic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That seems more like an Imbued Item. Idea is conveying &amp;quot;touch&amp;quot; via an energy medium, right? &amp;quot;Spooky action at a distance&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. We seem to be in agreement on the broad details. <br /> <br /> And honestly all I want is seeing a wizard sing along the storm, like that Gandalf vs. Saruman duel in the LotR movie (or was that cut out in the actual movie? Can\u2019t remember)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T21:33:08-07:00","id":1207876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1146419-alternate-arcana-attainments?p=1207757#post1207757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup. We seem to be in agreement on the broad details.<br /> <br /> And honestly all I want is seeing a wizard sing along the storm, like that Gandalf vs. Saruman duel in the LotR movie (or was that cut out in the actual movie? Can\u2019t remember)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that was fellowship of the ring. Also isn't that what Techne is for? e.g. Magic powered by symphonic speed metal.<br /> <br /> Edit: I've been using some home-brew attainments in my game. A Fate 4 greater utility attainment called &quot;Contract Lawyer&quot; which unsurprisingly has some quality of life effects for making and maintaining contracts. And a Matter 2 lesser utility attainment called &quot;Alchemist&quot; which uses your gnosis ritual casting time to prepare a potion. (It's sort of a hack until Signs of Sorcery)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","user":"Enlightened_Milkman","date":". 04-17-2018, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T17:14:55-07:00","id":1208251,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I think it would have been cool to see more effects like Time in a Bottle and Permanence (or even have Permanence not restricted to Matter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T13:37:56-07:00","id":1211132,"title":"","content":"I created a few Attainments for story driven purposes, as they were gifts of a Supernal Being my PC interacted with. <br /> <br /> <b>[Lesser Attainment]: Faerie's Eyes: </b>An Apprentice of Fate learns to see the Skeins of Fate in their most delicate and profound shapes; Destinies, and the crude manipulations of other Apprentices. A magician with this Attainment can sense the presence of Destiny in range through their Periphery, and with 1 Mana, can &quot;see&quot;the Destiny itself, knowing its details as well the accompanying Doom. In addition, they can also perceive Conditional spells, and know how to do undo/trigger them. <br /> <br /> <b>[Greater Attainment]: A Past Set in Stone:</b> An Adept of Time becomes a a solid form upon the mutable stream of Time. A mage with this Attainment may sense any attempts to alter their own timeline, and with 1 Mana, can resist the effect with a Potency equal to their Dots in Time. Mages with this Attainment are also constantly aware of alterations of Time around them, and if they could not before, can now discern Time Magic through their Peripheral Mage Sight. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}